# External custody must NEVER ship. The top-level path was NOT covered here,
# so fixtures/external/Codex and fixtures/external/codex-runtimes were tracked
# as symlinks to absolute paths on one developer's machine
# (/Users/archiepreston/Documents/Codex). No custody CONTENT was in the repo,
# but the layout of a private filesystem was, and the links are broken on every
# other machine. They are the local custody ACCESS mechanism and belong on disk,
# never in the index.
fixtures/external/
scripts/fixtures/external/

# EDGAR/XBRL/PDF corpus local custody (assets/corpus-plan.json tooling).
# Real filing bytes fetched from sec.gov/data.sec.gov land here. Custody
# CONTENT is public documents but stays out of the index by design: only
# sha256 hashes, locators and candidate inventories derived from it are ever
# referenced by the repository.
corpus-custody/

